-- title:
--   Ideals (b-ω^k) are generated by idempotents
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $\ell$ be a natural number with $1 < \ell$, and let $\omega \in R$ satisfy `IsPrimitiveRoot ω ℓ`, i.e. $\omega$ is a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity in $R$. Assume that the image of $\ell$ in $R$ is a unit, and that $\omega^i - \omega^j$ is a unit for all $i, j < \ell$ with $i \neq j$. Let $b \in R$ satisfy $b^{\ell} = 1$, and let $k$ be any natural number. Then there exists $e \in R$ with $e$ idempotent, $e \cdot e = e$, such that the principal ideals $\mathrm{span}\{b - \omega^k\}$ and $\mathrm{span}\{e\}$ of $R$ coincide. No bound $k < \ell$ is imposed: the exponent $k$ is an arbitrary natural number, $\omega^k$ being unchanged by reducing $k$ modulo $\ell$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Lagrange idempotents attached to an $\ell$-th root of unity in a ring in which $\ell$ is invertible generate the ideals cut out by the factors of $b^{\ell} - 1$; here it is used in the form 'the ideal $(b - \omega^k)$ is generated by an idempotent'. It is invoked in the analysis of the kernel of the classifying map for full level $\ell$ structures, where such an idempotent splitting of the moduli ring is what makes the kernel computable.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsPrimitiveRoot_exists_isIdempotentElem_span_sub_pow_eq.lean

